                <pb facs="0405" n="297" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg297"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/638a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-05-11T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 11, 1927—2
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>216. The Nationalist News Agency (Chinese) publishes telegram dated Hankow May 3,
                    stating Asiatic Petroleum Company operating Changsha under German management
                    until its own representative now returning to Changsha arrives.</p>
                <p>American firms restive under trade stoppage and Department is interested in any
                    attempts of other nationalities to continue or reopen commerce where Americans
                    have evacuated.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
